# nr-office-formula-lib-math: integration requirements, not yet compiled

## Ownership and registration

Only math.rs, logical.rs, information.rs, twin_math.rs, record-office-math.mjs and
fixtures/office-math are implemented by this leaf task. Do not replace another
library task's TABLES entries.

In native/core/crates/mixdog-xlsx-formula/src/functions/mod.rs, add:

    pub mod math;
    pub mod logical;
    pub mod information;

Append inside TABLES (retain every existing entry):

    math::FUNCTIONS,
    logical::FUNCTIONS,
    information::FUNCTIONS,

Each table is crate::Table; each implementation is fn(&[Value]) -> Result<Value, Failure>.
108 paths are enumerated from the original export list, category documentation and
function identities, including ERROR.TYPE, CEILINGMATH/FLOORMATH and ISO.CEILING's
nested variants. The coverage test requires exact equality with that enumeration.

## BLOCKING shared V8 primitive work (lead-owned; do not activate before this lands)

The current mixdog-js math.rs has exp/ln/pow/min/max/round but not the following
symbols called by this leaf. No platform-libm fallback was substituted. Searches
of this tree's native files found no bundled fdlibm or ieee754 source to reuse.
The existing math.rs documentation names V8 src/base/ieee754.cc as the reference.
Lead must provide/cache the corresponding authoritative source before porting;
this fragment does not authorize downloads.

Add to native/core/crates/mixdog-js/src/math.rs:

    pub fn abs(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn floor(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn ceil(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn sqrt(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn acos(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn asin(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn atan(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn atan2(x: f64, y: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn sin(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn cos(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn tan(x: f64) -> f64;
    pub fn random() -> f64;

abs/floor/ceil/sqrt must preserve V8 signed-zero/nonfinite behavior. Trig needs
V8-compatible reduction and fdlibm operations, not std::f64::sin/acos/etc.
atan2 arguments here are literally Math.atan2(x_num, y_num), including formulajs'
argument order. random supplies a production sample in [0,1); the twin injects
samples through math::with_random_sample and checks every result bit without
assuming the independent processes have the same random seed.

Add to mixdog-js/src/number.rs and re-export from mixdog-js/src/lib.rs:

    pub fn number_to_radix(number: f64, radix: f64) -> Result<String, String>;
    pub fn parse_int_radix(text: &str, radix: f64) -> f64;

number_to_radix is Number.prototype.toString(radix), including fractions and the
exact exception "toString() radix argument must be between 2 and 36" after JS
ToIntegerOrInfinity. parse_int_radix is JS parseInt(text, radix), including
ToInt32(radix), radix 0, hexadecimal prefixes, partial parses, signed zero and
nonfinite failures. BASE, DECIMAL, QUOTIENT and MUNIT consume these APIs. Avoid
replacing them with Rust format/parse rules.

No new dependency is added by this leaf. Any shared-helper dependency decision
belongs to the lead; no uncached dependency may be downloaded.

## Statistics library dependency

AGGREGATE and SUBTOTAL preserve the original dispatch (including AGGREGATE ignoring
its options argument). Their statistical branches call crate::registry::library()
for AVERAGE, COUNT, COUNTA, MAX, MIN, STDEV.S/P, VAR.S/P, MEDIAN, MODE.SNGL, LARGE,
SMALL, PERCENTILE.INC/EXC and QUARTILE.INC/EXC. These bodies belong to the statistics
task and must be registered before the complete twin or production usage. No
approximation or duplicate statistical implementation is provided here.

## Fixture index (lead-owned native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json)

Append to sets in ordered position:

{
    "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-math.mjs --tree <original tree>",
    "fileCount": 1,
    "manifest": "office-math/MANIFEST.json",
    "manifestSha256": "c0aa1798aa6eeae20f8d60065a0a81565fa87779d710f451f4ea73c7cfdb5d7d",
    "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-math.mjs",
    "set": "office-math",
    "totalBytes": 941536
}

The recorder verifies formulajs version 4.6.1, records its source SHA-256, encodes
IEEE-754 bits (including NaN and signed zero), dates, errors, undefined, arrays and
thrown messages. Arguments are cloned and encoded before calling mutation-prone
original functions. Each original call has a 1-second VM execution bound; a timeout
fails recording rather than being encoded as a successful expected answer.

Node reference execution completed: 108 paths, 4,282 cases. Rust was not compiled
or run. rustfmt only parsed/formatted the owned Rust sources.

## Verification gates

After shared helpers and all needed registrations land, run offline:

    cargo test -p mixdog-xlsx-formula --test twin_math --offline
    cargo test -p mixdog-xlsx-formula --test twin_engine --offline
    cargo clippy -p mixdog-xlsx-formula --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings

Every original result/error must match; there are no skipped functions or numeric
tolerances. twin_live_math is ignored only because it re-records with Node; the
normal coverage and result replay tests are not ignored. The existing formula-core
production-library integration test can then be enabled by its owner.

Residual limits requiring independent review: V8 recursion exhaustion for very
large FACT/FACTDOUBLE inputs depends on its stack/cache state; this port evaluates
finite factorials iteratively and reports the original stack exception for
nonterminating negative/nonfinite recursion. Date/array identity follows the
shared core Value representation. Extreme valid matrix/string allocations remain
subject to process memory, with fallible reservations where allocation is owned.
